    │   PKCS7; pycryptodomex is API-compatible with PyCrypto (same import paths), making it a near-drop-in
    │   replacement; cryptography requires rewriting the cipher construction; Fixed IV 
    │   (b'0000000000000000') is a security anti-pattern — should be random per encryption in any 
    │   migration
    ├── Constraints: crypto_required
    └── The code uses PyCrypto's AES in CBC mode with a fixed IV and null-byte padding. Both 
        'cryptography' (via hazmat.primitives.ciphers) and 'pycryptodomex' (drop-in replacement for 
        PyCrypto) provide equivalent AES-CBC functionality. PyCrypto is unmaintained and has HIGH-severity
        CVEs (GHSA-6528-wvf6-f6qg, GHSA-cq27-v7xp-c356), so migration is strongly recommended.

