└── async concurrency backend for monkey-patching stdlib
    ├── Candidates : gevent, eventlet
    ├── Used APIs  : monkey.patch_all
    ├── Pitfalls   : eventlet uses a different greenlet implementation; some C extensions may behave 
    │   differently; eventlet's WSGI server (eventlet.wsgi) has different performance characteristics than
    │   gevent.pywsgi; monkey patching order matters — must be done before any other imports in both cases
    └── gevent.monkey.patch_all() is used to monkey-patch the standard library (time.sleep, 
        threading.Thread, socket, etc.) for cooperative concurrency. eventlet provides an almost identical
        monkey.patch_all() API and is the canonical drop-in alternative for this purpose. Both are 
        greenlet-based coroutine libraries used to make synchronous Flask + SocketIO code run concurrently
        without rewriting to async/await.

