    └── The code uses netaddr.IPNetwork for IP network operations and type checking. Python's standard 
        library ipaddress module (available since Python 3.3) provides equivalent 
        IPNetwork/IPv4Network/IPv6Network classes with similar APIs for CIDR manipulation, containment 
        checks, and iteration. Since the code only uses IPNetwork class and basic isinstance checks, 
        ipaddress is a viable drop-in replacement.

