    │   `sentry_sdk.init(integrations=[FlaskIntegration()])`; raven's `setup_logging(SentryHandler)` is 
    │   replaced by `sentry_sdk.init(..., _experiments={'enable_logs': True})` or standard logging 
    │   integration; DSN configuration differs: raven reads from `SENTRY_DSN` env var automatically; 
    │   sentry-sdk requires explicit `dsn=` parameter or `SENTRY_DSN` env var; raven's `SentryHandler` 
    │   captured log records directly; sentry-sdk uses logging integration via `logging` module hooks
    └── raven is the legacy Sentry Python client (deprecated since 2018). sentry-sdk is the official 
        modern replacement with native Flask integration via 
        sentry_sdk.integrations.flask.FlaskIntegration. The code uses raven.contrib.flask.Sentry for Flask
        integration and raven.handlers.logging.SentryHandler for logging — both have direct equivalents in
        sentry-sdk.

